---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, SITE, formatDate } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Can’t Explain collects when you visit: Google Analytics for page views, no accounts, no mailing list. Plain language."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: we count page views with Google Analytics. We do not run accounts,
      ads, or a mailing list. The hall is a public git repo, not a dossier on you.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Updated {formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}.</p>

    <div class="notice">
      <strong>The even shorter version.</strong> If you just read the site, Google may
      see that a page loaded. If you email us, we have your email. If you open a GitHub
      issue, that is public. We do not sell any of it, mostly because there is almost
      nothing to sell.
    </div>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Every public page loads Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID{" "}
      <code>{SITE.gaMeasurementId}</code>). Google may set cookies and process the page
      URL, approximate location, device and browser, and the referring site. Google’s
      rules apply, not ours:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener">privacy policy</a>,
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245" rel="nofollow noopener"
        >Analytics data practices</a
      >.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Why:</strong> to see which cards people actually open, and which ones bounce.</li>
      <li><strong>What we look at:</strong> aggregates. Not “Colin from Mallacoota read the Gina card at 4pm.”</li>
      <li><strong>What we do not run:</strong> ads, heatmaps, session replay, marketing pixels.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can block the tag with a browser or extension. The hall still works. That is
      the whole point of a static site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="host">The host</h2>
    <p>
      Pages are served by Cloudflare. Like any CDN, it sees the technical facts of a
      request (IP address, URL, user-agent) to deliver the file. We do not keep a
      visitor database on top of that.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not">What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No logins, newsletters, or comment boxes.</li>
      <li>No fingerprinting of our own.</li>
      <li>
        Share buttons open X, Facebook, and the rest. Those companies see the click. We
        do not get a carbon copy.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="evidence">Evidence files</h2>
    <p>
      Captures under <code>/evidence/</code> are of sources that were already public.
      They are not a back door into anyone’s private life. If we got that wrong, email
      us.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Author:
      <a href="/about">Colin Dixon</a>. Also:
      <a href="/terms">terms</a>, <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>,
      <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
